# `@harmonia/common`

## Structure

```
src/
  schemas/{entity}/   index.ts, input.ts, output.ts, enum.ts
  utils/
    waitlist-token.ts   HMAC sign/verify for waitlist status URLs (uses HARMONIA_BETTER_AUTH_SECRET)
    waitlist-gate.ts    pure proxy gate decision (resolveWaitlistGate)
  services/
    brain/            classifier, embeddings, clustering, cluster-metadata, playlist-generator, track-matcher
    music/            spotify sync, lyrics fetching
    organize/         runOrganizeForUser, updateRun, checkCancelled, updateStageProgress
  trigger/tasks/
    organize.ts       parent orchestrator (calls all stages via .triggerAndWait())
    stages/           sync, lyrics, classify, embed, cluster, generate, match
  types/              pipeline progress types
```

Run tests: `pnpm --filter @harmonia/common test`

## Waitlist Utilities

- **`waitlist-token.ts`** — `signWaitlistStatusToken(email)` / `verifyWaitlistStatusToken(token)`; 90-day TTL; used by confirmation email URL and `orpc.waitlist.status`
- **`waitlist-gate.ts`** — `resolveWaitlistGate({ session, inviteCookie, pathname })` for dashboard `proxy.ts`

## Service Patterns

- Brain services take `(userId, onProgress?)` and return stage progress
- Each stage calls `onProgress` frequently so the dashboard progress bar updates live
- `updateStageProgress` uses JSONB `||` merge — safe for concurrent stages

## Service Safety Rules

- No inline raw SQL snippets in `@harmonia/common` services.
- Use typed Drizzle predicates/helpers exclusively for queries and mutations.
- If a DB operation seems to require raw SQL, redesign the implementation so it stays typed and schema-aware.
- For serialized DB string fields (for example `artistNames`), use a shared safe parser utility instead of inline `JSON.parse` calls.
- After schema changes, audit service queries for stale column references before merging.

## LLM Calls

All LLM calls resolve their model via `@harmonia/ai-provider`'s `getAIModel(task)` — never construct a provider client (`createGroq`, `createOpenAI`, etc.) directly in `@harmonia/common`. Each task is pinned to a fixed provider (`groq` | `concentrate`) via `TASK_PROVIDER`, not a global switch; gate on `isProviderConfigured(task)` before calling, and use `withLLMRetry()` for the shared 429-aware backoff instead of a bare `pRetry`. See `.cursor/rules/packages/00-package-index.mdc` § `@harmonia/ai-provider`.

Prompts are structured using `llml` from `@zenbase/llml`.

## Trigger.dev Tasks

```typescript
// Parent orchestrator
await syncStageTask.triggerAndWait({ userId, runId });
await lyricsStageTask.triggerAndWait({ userId, runId });
// ... etc (sequential, 7 stages total)
```

Each stage task: calls `checkCancelled` → sets `currentStage` → runs service → updates progress via `updateStageProgress`.

## Clustering Tuning (DBSCAN)

`CLUSTER_EPSILON` in `services/brain/clustering.ts` controls DBSCAN density for semantic-only embeddings (v2: no Title/Artists/Album). Embeddings are L2-normalised in-memory before clustering, so Euclidean distance is equivalent to cosine distance (for unit vectors, ‖a−b‖² = 2 − 2·cos(θ)) — the metric `text-embedding-3-small` and the `vector_cosine_ops` HNSW index on `track.embedding` both assume.

Epsilon in normalised-Euclidean units: `0.30` ≈ cos(θ) > ~0.95 (strict), `0.50` ≈ cos(θ) > ~0.87, `0.75` ≈ cos(θ) > ~0.72.

Tuning: clusters collapsing into a few mega-clusters → lower epsilon (try 0.20–0.25). Clusters too fragmented / mostly noise → raise it (try 0.35–0.45). The post-clustering sanity log (clusters/tracks ratio) makes regressions visible — re-tune against a representative library.

## Exports

All exports go through `packages/common/package.json` `exports` map. Add a new export entry when adding a new path.
